            "review_title": "Review at Pho Hien",
            "review_text": "Chloe J\n25 contributions\n0\nLocal secret\nApr 2019\nOur Australian friends who have been living in Ho Chi Minh for over a year, brought us to Pho Hien for the “best pho in Saigon” that isn’t yet brimming with tourists and food bloggers. \nWe have based many of our food choices in Vietnam on trip advisor reviews, which has led us to some pretty fantastic meals. That being said, it was refreshing to go somewhere that felt a bit more authentic, with limited English spoken, uncomfortable crammed stools, and tables loaded with addictive and delicious chilli sauces, lime, fresh chilli and loads of Thai Basil to customise you’re steaming bowl of flavourful and intense beef pho. \nThe prices are very reasonable, and the food delicious. Would definitely recommend to anyone looking for a great pho experience.\nRead more\nWritten April 13, 2019",
